    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today with a clear top-tier anchor in **Kyle Tucker** (85.90), whose matchup against Ryan Feltner offers significant upside despite the 37% rain risk. Alongside **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) provides excellent value against a high-xERA opponent in Ray, benefiting from a massive +19% boost due to the starter's poor projected command. **Andy Pages** (74.43) rounds out the high-efficiency trio, as he capitalizes on a favorable park factor and a premium #3 spot in the lineup. These starters are heavily leveraged to exploit poor pitching environments, which is essential for maintaining our aggressive 5x5 pace.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages and park factors have elevated the stocks of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (68.66). Both hitters benefit from a +16% park adjustment, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** effectively neutralizing his right-handed opponent to command a starting spot at 1B. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Wade Meckler** (54.93); while he offers a high floor due to his top-of-the-order positioning and a favorable matchup against the struggling Cristian Javier, the overall efficiency scores of the outfield starters edged him out. **Wade Meckler** remains the primary pivot if the rain clouds over the **Kyle Tucker** or **Andy Pages** games lead to a postponement.\n\nWe remain vigilant regarding the lineup status of **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**, all of whom are currently modeled on assumed batting orders. While **Nasim Nunez** (59.42) remains in the lineup despite a lower order position, his efficiency is propped up by a rare combination of SP-specific speed factors, keeping him in the mix to chase our precious stolen base categories. As we navigate the day, the health of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remains a limiting factor on our depth, making the performance of our utility options\u2014including **Miguel Vargas** and the sidelined **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014critical to our long-term cap management.",
